(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"70308805-93b5-439d-b908-602ace6f71a6"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"64a248e5-771c-479a-a975-c1d8f2d4221d"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"609dfc5a-a149-4f1c-94ca-1f0adc787324"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"98559c37-ddcb-41b8-ae1c-10be65a3d9dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"629fe94e-e4d3-4b77-a8de-83b1739d39a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bc349e6d-cd7b-49c1-95d8-410814413e70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7fd1cb57-9502-46a4-821f-f16a240d9258"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2ea55ab0-a67f-4314-9c4c-7286676eef42"],

Cell["\<\
The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette also \
sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output matches the \
screen.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d09a354f-0a71-47f9-b8fa-08200d50b247"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"93f1f4f6-c0d0-4e19-bdce-41094d1eb64c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"358e9bbe-20b6-4486-a896-384de627f1b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c7bf78f4-9fbd-479d-bebc-4f1931fa774c"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"430cf451-daee-496f-b223-dd96093fbe3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"57a4725c-843a-41e2-9076-3f2fde875127"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2c87a6cc-a26c-4e27-a699-af8bb4114503"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4e8fda4f-5355-4ecc-ada5-7ab552c4be17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tag cell",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " names a cell, and ",
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inserts a red bracketed link to that name \[LongDash] the two together \
give a bibliography: style each entry ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tag it, cite it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d93bc54b-ce29-4818-ba72-756015b2d7ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c11c1b50-eb1e-45b3-a4b1-d0db731c5d5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2a049b97-702f-492d-bb57-c576500eb5bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a bibliography tagged before that was true \[LongDash] or tagged \
through the Cell Tags dialog rather than the palette \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " labels every entry of a notebook at once, and clears the label of an entry \
whose tag you removed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fdf0c319-6264-466f-a867-40e59fd0e344"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Existing tags are listed under ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d7eb4baf-6ecb-4924-8ce2-d4436950dbad"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"da46390f-264e-4b02-b8e6-2ab1a9f18f88"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"e9e9ab37-0c5d-4f56-be25-de8c6572d878"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"d6b25f55-e34c-\
40d1-9a4a-7b8b2514b924"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5d2e98f0-138a-4fe3-b0cb-104936d288c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d60cfd73-6533-456b-b154-1807c94f1638"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"796d4559-9724-47b0-a8cf-125d019f33d2"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1b6aac1f-ec92-4cf0-826a-2bbe5ed984e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"28826ae1-e8c9-4ed8-ad16-c719f91c334e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0174b872-627a-4dcb-8493-7dac75086210"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2d20e8eb-8b99-461d-b8cc-4c922981e8ba"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1fb43214-9b03-4144-93af-56790361abcf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0e5e902f-f4bc-46e1-89a0-922d52e92f98"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the rest of the prose with it \[LongDash] the title, the \
headings, the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography \
entries, and both kinds of list \[LongDash] so the document keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"737285a6-ae27-40a4-9fa1-7b24bc5d12e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8aaffae7-8c21-403f-8809-110145861cea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"872f5928-ff23-4aaf-bdad-688909a828cb"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"04dbbcce-8727-4e85-bf19-f27af73bcd25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a59d1a95-e927-4529-ab1c-9fc6e3de017b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2000192d-49c2-41c7-baa4-bdec080b02e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"23b73c12-3158-4c1f-86de-c5e044c3accb"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cad7838f-1277-4efc-b464-ae983b173fb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"401e6a9d-f203-42a8-9d93-6dc2b694ba67"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"06b7932e-2fff-45c9-a75b-c44a931b7fc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f390ee84-0b71-40ed-b326-8409ed7d62ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1ad44e87-f8e9-4687-9876-eaca3804810a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4f029d1e-832a-42bf-ab60-7f021f7b8caa"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d0711d9e-c56c-4e74-aaeb-899e7030d683"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4c30a851-53d4-49d7-8889-98eb3e69616e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1706ac7a-21d1-4b1e-b9da-5dd9734ea07b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fcf7016f-dbc5-44ea-9d94-b75f47948cf8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"988d1736-3c33-4fa9-961c-9f7e15099034"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6617193e-0d80-4b88-8d51-f1e16e293924"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"25ad7546-ce2f-4c2a-8bc7-da7045f43bae"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b691cc23-ced9-49de-90d1-72338146334b"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a279d4f4-4887-4b7a-a820-d2cb0bc0d07e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select the cells to convert, then press ",
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". With nothing selected the whole notebook is converted."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b6a7af75-40c0-4503-bb6e-8a0e16f4cbe6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a8d2eb4f-05b3-4166-9486-1e05a783ae47"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e6e30903-0764-428d-9f03-7c1e37be96cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3b1e0a8b-9bdb-41fe-8a6c-9df227d3776b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"71d620e8-3e3a-4396-9da0-1ff060293898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe. To bring in a LaTeX paper, paste it as Text cells and \
convert."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4a44692d-8a90-4b28-ab7c-28c641df2edc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ImportLaTeXDocument[\"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads a whole paper instead: ",
 StyleBox["\\section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the theorem-like environments the preamble declares become cells of \
the matching style, and ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXDocument",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes it back out. Lists, figures and front matter are carried verbatim, \
so what it does not convert it also does not damage."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9ea09e5d-8801-449d-86de-ac9e4664a8c1"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6eb5ab98-f40c-4b64-a7e3-b99648d09305"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the MaTeX buttons; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do \
not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a0f8caf2-4b81-45bd-939a-82bf951bdebc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e2d6d4a5-8f59-4749-82fb-880996bbe2f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d89c3650-726e-4ec0-90d4-3584b3786c50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " renders the selected display equations through LaTeX; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " restores editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0220f06c-61c9-4ca0-b5a1-acd6b325cab5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"10947b69-7fb3-48d4-8d15-d06460f9e921"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3dbe01e4-9204-408a-b659-b3a83e851979"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b4c3dc7e-3316-4268-b68d-b01b4d8fd0c5"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bc93d400-d1cb-460c-9cae-be584faf9a87"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5558d809-42bd-4a34-b70f-67ec0cac7ce8"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bc56e3e8-8f1d-46ba-9ee9-1c1f1f2695a8"],

Cell["\<\
Convert to LaTeX at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the \
notebook is the source.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b37cbc78-3524-460d-8eca-d16479be0b31"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and convert MaTeX cells back to math so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"eb999931-598e-40fb-b95c-7cb4a4820764"],

